From 73af29667d3c5a9eca1bc0a71bddd99f8f2e210c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:51:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/49] x86_64/fpu/587: accurate sin, cos, tan and sincos

The x87 fsin, fcos and fptan are inaccurate (large errors for big
arguments; about 800 failures in math/test-double and test-float).  Use
the generic dbl-64 and flt-32 implementations like i386 and drop the
empty stubs that kept the dbl-64 helpers out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
